    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41080" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Rĕmŭlus</span></b> ,
			i, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>a proper name.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Remulus Silvius, <i>a king of Alba</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 14,
				616</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. F. 4, 49 sq.</span></i> (called Romulus
			Silvius, <i><span class="en">Liv. 1, 3</span></i>).— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> For <i>Remus</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Sulp. Sat. 19</span></i>; cf. 2.
			Remus.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A name of fictitious heroes</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 9,
				360</span></i>; <i><span class="en">593</span></i>; <i><span class="en">633</span></i>; 11, 636; <i><span class="en">Sil. 4,
			186</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
